=== 3. Four Two-Query Encryption-Only Splice Variants on COLM_0 (colm0v1/ref) ===
-------------------------------------------------------------------
== COLM splice forgery -- variant 'fade' -- implementation tag stride 0 ==
message 1: l1 = 130 blocks (2080 bytes; last block 16 byte(s) -- COMPLETE), AD1 = 32 bytes, no intermediate tags
splice index set I0 = {1,2,3,8,129}   [derived at run time from GF(2^128)]
queries: 2 ENCRYPTION, 0 decryption, 0 verification, 0 RUP.  nonces distinct (nonce-respecting).
addendum Theorem 2 at q=2, s=1, a=2, l=130 : sigma=396 sigma_auth=398
  its own bound  9*sigma_auth^2/2^n + s/2^n = 4.189571e-33 = 2^-107.56
  measured forging advantage                = 1  (deterministic)

KAT-1 honest round trip of the implementation's own ciphertext : PASS (ret=0 mlen=2080, clen=2096)
KAT-2 one flipped ciphertext bit is REJECTED                   : PASS (ret=-1)
      common ciphertext prefix of the two queries: 0 bytes = 0 blocks
      forgery non-trivial (differs from query 1's output)        : yes
      forgery tag block == query 1's tag block (verbatim reuse)  : yes  <-- addendum Lemma 3 'good forge view' condition 2 violated DELIBERATELY
      crypto_aead_decrypt(forgery) ret=0 -> ACCEPTED
      recovered plaintext differs from the queried message in 2071 / 2080 bytes (so the forgery is not a replay)

trials = 25   forgeries ACCEPTED = 25   trivial = 0   tag-block reused = 25
negative control 1 (DROP the middle element of I0)   accepted 0 / 25
negative control 2 (ADD one block not in I0)         accepted 0 / 25
negative control 3 (RANDOM 5-block splice sets)    accepted 0 / 200   <- statistical baseline
EXPECTATION for this build: every splice is ACCEPTED, every control REJECTED
RESULT: SUCCESS
